---
source: crates/fossil-graph/tests/schemas.rs
expression: "schema_for! (discovery::ReadParams)"
---
$schema: "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
title: ReadParams
description: "Rows of one vertex type, filtered, ordered and capped.\n\n**`where` is SQL and is trusted exactly as far as `execute_sql` is**, which is why its type is [`RawSql`] and why this struct is not `Deserialize`: the permission that opens the escape hatch is the same token that fills this field, and [`Operation::from_wire`](super::Operation::from_wire) is the one place either can be built from wire JSON. [`raw_sql`](super::raw_sql) carries the argument."
type: object
required:
  - vertex_type
properties:
  descending:
    default: false
    type: boolean
  limit:
    default: 100
    type: integer
    format: uint32
    minimum: 0
  order_by:
    description: "Column to order by. Absent, the rows arrive in storage order, which is the writer's Morton order and says nothing the caller asked about."
    default: ~
    type:
      - string
      - "null"
  vertex_type:
    type: string
  where:
    description: "A `WHERE` predicate over the type's columns, without the keyword. Reading one vertex is `subject = '…'`."
    default: ~
    type:
      - string
      - "null"
additionalProperties: false
